BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 790 Td 14.5 TL (ILLUSTRATIVE TEXT FOR TESTING - NOT AN OFFICIAL RWANDA FDA DOCUMENT) Tj T* () Tj T* (GUIDELINES ON THE RELIANCE REGISTRATION PATHWAY FOR HUMAN MEDICINES) Tj T* (Version 2026-01) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. Purpose) Tj T* (A human medicine already approved by a reference regulatory authority may be registered) Tj T* (through the reliance pathway. Rwanda FDA relies on the reference authority's assessment and) Tj T* (inspection, so the applicant must prove that the product submitted is the same product.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. Reference regulatory authorities) Tj T* (Accepted reference authorities include the European Medicines Agency, the US Food and Drug) Tj T* (Administration, the MHRA, Swissmedic, Health Canada, the TGA, WHO Prequalification and the) Tj T* (EAC joint assessment.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3. Declaration of sameness) Tj T* (The applicant submits a declaration of sameness, following the Rwanda FDA template. It) Tj T* (states the reference authority and the product's registration number with that authority,) Tj T* (names the manufacturing site, and declares that the product submitted to Rwanda FDA is) Tj T* (identical to the approved product in formulation, manufacturing site, manufacturing process,) Tj T* (specifications and packaging. It is signed and dated by the marketing authorization holder.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4. GMP certificate) Tj T* (A Good Manufacturing Practice certificate issued by the reference regulatory authority must) Tj T* (be submitted for every manufacturing site. It must name the site and must be valid on the) Tj T* (date of submission. Certificates issued by other authorities are not accepted for this) Tj T* (pathway.) Tj T* () Tj T* (5. Letter of authorization) Tj T* (The applicant submits a letter, following the Rwanda FDA template, authorizing the reference) Tj T* (regulatory authority to share its assessment and inspection reports about the product with) Tj T* (Rwanda FDA. A letter that only confirms the product's approval is not sufficient.) Tj T* ET
endstream
